# Structural tokens for the JSON documents `wasm_disc` feeds
# `serde_json::from_slice::<bdinfo_rs_wasm::mirror::Disc>`.
#
# Every entry is a literal serde_json's own parser matches an input byte range
# against — the three value keywords it compares verbatim, and the punctuation
# runs that open and close an object, an array and a member. Field NAMES are
# deliberately absent: they are the shape libFuzzer's comparison tracing already
# recovers unaided, and `disc-fields.dict` records what writing them down was
# measured to be worth.
#
# Value extremes (`u64::MAX` sizes, `1e308` lengths) are not here either. They
# are not literals any parser compares against, so they belong in a seed —
# `corpus/wasm_disc/saturated` carries them.

"null"
"true"
"false"
"{\""
"\":"
"\":\""
"\",\""
"\":["
"\":[{\""
"\"}"
"\"}]"
"}]}"
"[]"
"{}"
"\":{\""
"},{\""
